@startuml Canceled Checkout Flow
!theme plain
title Stripe Payment - Canceled Checkout Flow

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Customer as C
participant "PaymentController" as PC
participant "ContractService" as CS
participant "EventDispatcher" as ED
participant "StripeCheckoutSessionHandler" as SCSH
participant "Stripe API" as S
participant "Cron Job" as CRON
database "Database" as DB

== Phase 1: Initiate Checkout ==

C -> PC: Select Stripe Payment
activate PC

PC -> CS: createContract(userId, basket)
activate CS
CS -> DB: Save contract (PENDING)
CS --> PC: PaymentContract
deactivate CS

PC -> ED: dispatch(StripeCheckoutSessionRequestEvent)
activate ED

ED -> SCSH: handle(event)
activate SCSH

SCSH -> S: checkout.sessions.create({...})
activate S
S --> SCSH: CheckoutSession (cs_xxx)
deactivate S

SCSH -> DB: Update contract with session_id
SCSH --> ED: context.set('checkoutUrl')
deactivate SCSH

ED --> PC: Event processed
deactivate ED

PC --> C: Redirect to Stripe Checkout
deactivate PC

== Phase 2: Customer Cancels ==

C -> S: View Stripe Checkout page
note right of C
  Customer decides not to pay:
  - Clicks browser back button
  - Closes the tab
  - Clicks "Back" link on Stripe
end note

S --> C: Redirect to cancel_url\n(index.php?cl=payment)

== Phase 3: Return to Payment Page ==

C -> PC: GET /payment (cancel_url)
activate PC

note over PC
  **No event fired**

  Customer simply returns
  to payment selection.

  Contract remains PENDING.
end note

PC --> C: Payment selection page\n(can select different method or retry)
deactivate PC

== Phase 4: Contract Cleanup (Later) ==

note over CRON, DB
  Contract has TTL (e.g., 30 minutes)
  Cron job runs periodically
end note

CRON -> CS: cleanupExpiredContracts()
activate CS
CS -> DB: Find contracts where\ncreatedAt + TTL < now\nAND state = PENDING
DB --> CS: [contract_xxx]
CS -> DB: Update state: EXPIRED
CS --> CRON: Cleaned up 1 contract
deactivate CS

== Alternative: Customer Retries ==

C -> PC: Select Stripe Payment again
activate PC
note over PC
  Can use same contract
  if not expired,
  OR create new contract
end note
PC --> C: Redirect to Stripe Checkout
deactivate PC

== Result ==

note over C, DB #FFEEEE
  ⚠️ No order created
  ⚠️ Contract expires after TTL
  ⚠️ Stripe Checkout Session expires after 24h
  ✅ Customer can retry anytime
  ✅ No payment was charged
end note

@enduml
